---
// logging's four parts, in the order a record meets them (text of the post: a
// logger is what code calls, a filter adds or changes fields, a handler decides
// where the line goes, a formatter decides what it looks like).
const W = 900, H = 290, by = 70, bh = 56, bw = 124;
const row = [
  { cx: 90, name: 'logger', en: 'what code calls', vi: 'thứ code gọi' },
  { cx: 270, name: 'filter', en: 'adds or changes fields', vi: 'thêm hoặc đổi field', red: true },
  { cx: 450, name: 'handler', en: 'decides where it goes', vi: 'quyết định đi đâu' },
  { cx: 630, name: 'stdout', en: 'the destination here', vi: 'đích ở bài này' },
];
---
<figure class="bep10l">
  <div class="bep10l-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Four parts of Python logging. A logger, which code calls, passes the record to a filter that adds or changes fields, then to a handler that decides where the line goes, here stdout. A formatter below the handler decides what the line looks like. The filter is drawn in red because it is where the request id is added.">
    {row.map((r, i) => (
      <g>
        <rect x={r.cx - bw / 2} y={by} width={bw} height={bh} rx="8" class={r.red ? 'boxr' : 'box'} />
        <text x={r.cx} y={by + 33} text-anchor="middle" class="b"><tspan data-lang-en>{r.name}</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>{r.name}</tspan></text>
        <text x={r.cx} y={by + bh + 26} text-anchor="middle" class="m"><tspan data-lang-en>{r.en}</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>{r.vi}</tspan></text>
        {i < row.length - 1 && <line x1={r.cx + bw / 2 + 6} y1={by + bh / 2} x2={row[i + 1].cx - bw / 2 - 14} y2={by + bh / 2} class="ln" />}
        {i < row.length - 1 && <polygon points={`${row[i + 1].cx - bw / 2 - 14},${by + bh / 2 - 6} ${row[i + 1].cx - bw / 2 - 2},${by + bh / 2} ${row[i + 1].cx - bw / 2 - 14},${by + bh / 2 + 6}`} class="arrow" />}
      </g>
    ))}
    <line x1="450" y1={by + bh + 40} x2="450" y2="196" class="ln" />
    <rect x={450 - bw / 2} y="196" width={bw} height={bh} rx="8" class="box" />
    <text x="450" y="229" text-anchor="middle" class="b"><tspan data-lang-en>formatter</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>formatter</tspan></text>
    <text x="528" y="229" class="m"><tspan data-lang-en>decides what it looks like: one JSON object per line</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>quyết định hình dạng: mỗi dòng một object JSON</tspan></text>
    <text x="40" y="40" class="h"><tspan data-lang-en>One log call, four parts</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Một lệnh log, bốn phần</tspan></text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>The same four parts exist in every Python service. The filter is the one the rest of the post keeps using: it stamps the request id, and later scrubs secrets.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Bốn phần này có trong mọi service Python. Filter là phần các mục sau dùng đi dùng lại: nó đóng dấu request id, rồi sau đó che secret.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .bep10l { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .bep10l-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .bep10l svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .bep10l text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .bep10l .h { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); font-size: 15px; }
  .bep10l .m { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .bep10l .b { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .bep10l .r { fill: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }
  .bep10l .box { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .bep10l .boxr { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .bep10l .ln { stroke: var(--text-faint); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .bep10l .lnr { stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .bep10l .axis { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 2; }
  .bep10l .arrow { fill: var(--text-faint); }
  .bep10l .arrowr { fill: var(--red); }
  .bep10l figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
